## 📂 Workbook Structure

The project workbook contains three main sheets:

### 1. `Cleaned_Data`

Contains the processed airfare dataset with **11,536 records** and 32 fields.

Important fields include:

- Quote ID
- Scrape Timestamp
- Source Name
- Origin
- Destination
- Route
- Travel Date
- Advance Purchase Days
- Booking Window
- Airline
- Flight Number
- Departure Time
- Arrival Time
- Duration
- Stops
- Fare Class
- Base Fare
- Taxes
- Convenience Fee
- Total Fare
- Availability
- Status
- Outlier Flag
- Duplicate Flag
- Missing Value Flag
- Exclusion Flag

---

### 2. `Automated_Report`

This sheet provides automatically summarized airfare statistics.

### Key KPIs

| Metric | Value |
|---|---:|
| Total Valid Records | 11,536 |
| Average Fare | ₹17,564.81 |
| Minimum Fare | ₹16,800.09 |
| Maximum Fare | ₹18,388.44 |
| Number of Airlines | 5 |
| Number of Routes | 6 |

The report also contains:

- Average fare by airline
- Top routes by average fare
- Average fare by number of stops
- Flight record counts

---

### 3. `Visual_Summaries`

This sheet contains summarized data used for visual analysis.

The visual analysis includes:

- Airline-wise average airfare
- Travel-date-wise average airfare
- Route-level comparisons
- Fare patterns based on stops

These summaries make it easier to identify patterns and compare airfare values.

